OpenWings patch 0027: OpenWings names wherever people look

The settings, browser storage, cookies, headers and references a person or
an administrator sees carry OpenWings names. Every earlier name is still read,
so an upgrade loses nothing and signs nobody out; the source files keep their
internal identifiers (module names, environment reads, stored column and
collection names), which nobody sees.

  * routes/auth_routes.py, app.py: the session cookie is openwings_session.
    The earlier cookie is still accepted, and the first request that brings
    it gets the same session under the new name (and the old one cleared).
  * static/js/openwings-storage.js (new), static/index.html, static/login.html,
    routes/search/search_routes.py: one small script, loaded first, moves
    browser storage keys saved under the earlier prefixes to openwings-* and
    ow-* once (nothing is lost: theme, layout, saved sign-in name), and lets
    the app's scripts keep their own key literals. Page source of the two
    main pages names no upstream; globals renamed across static/.
  * static/sw.js: cache openwings-v662-names (the old cache is deleted on
    activate, as before).
  * routes/chat_routes.py, static/js/chat.js: X-OpenWings-Run-Id (the earlier
    header is still accepted on stop and finish).
  * Mail the app sends carries X-OpenWings-Origin/Kind/Ref (email_routes,
    email_pollers, task_scheduler, note_routes); reminders and the urgent-mail
    scanner still recognise mail sent with the earlier headers. Webhooks carry
    X-OpenWings-Event and X-OpenWings-Signature. Copilot's default
    User-Agent and editor version say OpenWings/1.0.
  * Attachment references shown to the model are openwings://attachment/ID;
    the earlier scheme is still accepted everywhere one is read.
  * routes/codex_routes.py, static/js/settings.js: the Codex and Claude agent
    bundles download as openwings-*.zip with an openwings folder, plugin id,
    helper script and OPENWINGS_URL / OPENWINGS_API_TOKEN, and the setup
    commands in Settings match.
  * routes/email/email_routes.py, email_helpers.py: the API docs list
    /api/email/app/reminders, /api/email/compose-from-library(-zip) and the
    field mail_kind; the earlier paths and field name keep working (hidden).
  * Texts that reach people or the model: the companion's server name, the
    reserved names in the sign-in policy, the run_script description, two
    error messages (encryption key, private CalDAV), the MCP allow-list hint,
    the Cookbook's MLX bridge hints and recipes, the inline-code font token
    written into documents and mail (the earlier token is still recognised),
    console messages.
  * setup.py: its three messages about the admin account name OPENWINGS_*.
  * routes/diagnostics_routes.py: the server log in Settings shows OPENWINGS_*
    setting names and plain index names, also in lines written earlier.
  * tests/: upstream tests that check the renamed cookie, headers, references,
    script names and cache name now expect the new ones.
  * core/database.py: task notifications stored under the earlier default
    sender name show "OpenWings" (one idempotent UPDATE at start).

